  <process id="proc_unstated" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>pm:Stack of `unstated`. This document shows how the stack's layers and operations connect, and none of its figures. How much of the system the stack holds is stated on the laneSet. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/pools.sqlc]</documentation>
    <laneSet id="lanes_unstated" name="draw">
      <documentation>scope: scoped. `complete` says there are no other layers of this system, `scoped` says somebody established what lies outside and left it out, `unbounded` says nobody looked. A lane set has no way to say which, so this sentence is the only place it is said. The filing's reason: one layer, on purpose: this filing exists to show a subject that is not a supply, and the entity plainly has others [assets/sqlc/diagrams/scopes.sqlc]</documentation>
      <documentation>coupling search: notApplicable. `unmeasured` means nobody looked, `none` means somebody looked and found no dependence, `notApplicable` means there is no pair to couple, and `stated` means the dependences drawn here. An absent line is not independence. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/searches.sqlc]</documentation>
      <lane id="lane_unstated_margin-ratio" name="margin-ratio">
        <documentation>rank 0: the number of levels of parts beneath this layer. At 0 it waits on nothing; above 0 it waits for every part below it to arrive [assets/sqlc/rank/evaluation_order.sqlc]</documentation>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <textAnnotation id="note_unstated_lane">
      <text>An empty lane is a layer nothing draws on, not an idle one: every layer carries figures, and BPMN has no glyph to show them. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/lane_grain.sqlc]</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <textAnnotation id="note_unstated_scope">
      <text>Scope: scoped. The pool is the whole system only when the filing says `complete`. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/scopes.sqlc]</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <textAnnotation id="note_unstated_search">
      <text>Coupling search: notApplicable. An absent dependence line is not independence. [assets/sqlc/diagrams/searches.sqlc]</text>
    </textAnnotation>
  </process>
